      "writtenOn": "2025-02-14T23:22:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In Dawn\u0027s native implementation, class `BufferBase`\u0027s inheriance chain is:\nBufferBase -\u003e SharedResource -\u003e ApiObjectBase -\u003e ObjectBase -\u003e ErrorMonad -\u003e RefCounted.\n\nIn `ApiObjectBase::DeleteThis()`, `Destroy()` is called:\n\n```\n// src\\dawn\\native\\ObjectBase.cpp\nvoid ApiObjectBase::DeleteThis() {\n    Destroy();\n    RefCounted::DeleteThis();\n}\n\n```\n\n`DeleteThis()` is called in `RefCounted::Release`:\n```\n// src\\dawn\\common\\RefCounted.cpp\nvoid RefCounted::Release() {\n    if (mRefCount.Decrement()) {\n        DeleteThis();\n    }\n}\n\n```\n\nEmWgpu\u0027s implementation does not have this. And the call to `Destroy()` is never happened unless user explicitly call `buffer.destroy()`. In JavaScript webgpu API, only `device` and `buffer` exposes `destroy` to users.\n\nEmWgpu\u0027s implementation of device also have refcount problem, but I will not discuss about it since this PR is for buffer.",
      "parentUuid": "f7380efb_f463899c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 0,
